VERDICT: FIX-THEN-SHIP
FINDINGS:
🟠 [station-id-qualify-third-seat] MUST-FIX Finding-id qualification is only applied to the FIRST colliding seat pair: in runPanel's merge, when a third seat reports the same finding_id with yet another digest, the `prior.qualified` branch re-qualifies the first occurrence and qualifies the current one (`s<seatIndex>.<id>`), but a digest matching the FIRST seat's digest while differing from the second's is silently deduped against the Map key (unqualified `dup-1` vs `s1.dup-1` vs a missing `s2.dup-1`), so disposition registries keyed on `unresolved_findings` can carry an unqualified id that two seats disagree on — violating §1.1.1 "when two seats report the same finding_id with different digests, the station qualifies BOTH by seat index". Smallest remediation: track per-seat digests in the Map (array of {seatIndex,digest}) and qualify every occurrence whenever any digest differs, or state/pin three-seat collision behavior in a test.
🟠 [station-panel-journal-generation] MUST-FIX In runPanel, station panel REVIEW_COMPLETED events are journaled with `generation: reviewInput.repair_generation`, but the composition's reviewPanel call does not pass `repair_generation` in reviewPayload (the single-seat path gets it via the same payload — verify at base), so every station panel records `generation: undefined` and `stageIdentity: campaign-review-panel:n`, corrupting the per-generation review event journal the engine's stagnation/gate-attempt accounting reads. Smallest remediation: include `repair_generation` in the reviewPanel dispatch payload (or accept 0 explicitly) and pin it in the station test.
🟠 [station-reuse-packet-null] MUST-FIX stationPanelReuse requires `hasOwnProperty(lastReview,'packet_hash')`, and composition sets `packet_hash: fullDiff.packet_hash || null` — so a station panel whose seats produced no packet_hash (runPanel only sets packet_hash when packetHashesConsistent && length>0) leaves lastReview.packet_hash === null which PASSES the hasOwnProperty check, and terminal reuse then fires on identity "null === null" even when the spec requires reuse "for the same … packet identity"; a stale/absent packet identity silently reuses the in-loop panel. Smallest remediation: require `typeof lastReview.packet_hash === 'string' && isCanonicalSha256(lastReview.packet_hash)` (and compare against the terminal packet hash when present) before stationPanelReuse.
🟠 [below-quorum-test-weak] MUST-FIX The `station_below_quorum` case asserts only `reviewCalls === 0` and `status !== 'converged'`; it never asserts the 2-B reason (`final_panel_below_minimum` / `final_panel_families_below_minimum` / seat-fault durable wait with one row per seat), so the acceptance criterion `station-safety` (blocked/parked with the 2-B reason) is not actually pinned — a regression that blocks with a generic reason would pass. Smallest remediation: assert the concrete 2-B reason string and the AWAITING_DISPOSITION/blocked phase in the test.
🔵 [station-snapshot-station-ignored] CUT/FOLLOW-UP runPanel resolves the live station via `resolveReviewStation(roster)` when rebuilding liveSnap, while the composition gate reads `campaignControl.qc_panel_snapshot.review_station`; a live roster flip is caught as rosterDrift (digest mismatch) so behavior is fail-visible, matching the drift design — hardening to read the sealed value directly is optional and excluded.
🔵 [schema-key-order-brittle] CUT/FOLLOW-UP The resolver EXPECTED_KEYS pin and printf format-string arg alignment for the new `in_rail_review` slot are verified by the parity test but remain a hand-maintained ordering; excluded as existing pattern.
NO-FINDING-PROOF: omitted (FIX-THEN-SHIP)
